Track 3: Did the Pollen Catch Fire?
- Story & Context: Legend says that during the Great Equinox trade at Outpost Nine, an overloaded synth battery ignited an entire greenhouse dome filled with blooming night-cereus, turning the horizon into a pillar of white flame. Instead of fleeing, the band stayed on their wooden risers, using the bellowing accordion to pump thick, jasmine-scented smoke through their open oscillator filters while playing at a breakneck fusion tempo. Desert patrol guards ten miles away reported hearing crystal-clear indie harmonies floating on the thermal draft: "We planted voltage in the sand and watched the orchids bloom backwards." The charred clearing where the tent once stood remains a pilgrimage site, where wind blowing through empty glass panes still hums the song's opening minor-ninth chord.
